  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat, with a screenshot of v0.19.0 bb5ecc43): \"Bug, when choosing slot like this and two edges the slot should stay withing the selection, in this case just two edges is selected as well so its not confined.\"\n\nWhat happens: a Slot operation with two edges selected (Chain Body1, open, 50.0 mm, 1 of 2 and 2 of 2: the two long edges of the pocket floor) still takes its shape from the typed endpoints A (-20, 0), B (20, 0) and the slot width (4.0 mm). The selection is ignored: the preview outline runs from the pocket across the pocket wall into the solid part of the model. The page says \"Boundary settings do not apply to it: a Slot is authored by its two endpoints and width\". (Generate was refused here only because the 4 mm slot is narrower than the 6 mm tool; with a wider slot nothing confines it.)\n\nExpected:\n- With edges (or a face) selected, the slot is derived from the selection and stays inside it: two opposite edges give the slot between them (centre line, length and width from the edges); a face gives the slot that fits that face. The typed endpoints and width are then the result shown, or are limited to the selected region.\n- A slot that does not fit inside the selection, or that would cut the model, is refused by name with the numbers. It is never generated or previewed across a wall as if it were fine.\n- With nothing selected, the typed endpoints still work, and the model gouge check still decides.\n\nRelated: issue 1503 (the Trochoidal slot has the same fault and cuts into the model while reporting OK). The two share the endpoint-and-width authoring and should share the fix.\n\nDone means: a test with two selected pocket edges gives a slot inside the pocket; a slot longer or wider than the selection is refused by name; a slot through the model wall never posts; the preview outline matches what is generated; undo, the MCP parameters and the structural UI test cover the selection-driven slot.\n",
